{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Land the operator-approved code-review criteria threshold flips derived from the code-v3 sidecar calibration. The analysis is COMPLETE (see this ticket's comments: 1760 code_review_result_v2 sidecars / 1173 changes / 4359 findings, calibrated per-criterion, precision-first). This ticket lands the recommendation the operator has cleared.\n\n## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` currently blocks only on the two DET security detectors + the `security` AGENT criterion (b9c0). Every other LLM criterion is advisory@0.95, so high-precision defect classes the code-v3 corpus shows are safe to block (validity>=0.95 on every would-block finding, low change-blocking volume) never gate a review. The calibration recommended flipping four to blocking; the operator has approved landing them.\n\n## Approach\nEdit the packaged `criteria_routing.json` to flip exactly four criteria from advisory to blocking at their calibrated thresholds, each annotated with a `_comment` citing this ticket + the code-v3 calibration:\n- api-compat -> blocking @ 0.51 (n=118, validity 0.88; break-in-caller API changes, high-precision/low-volume)\n- deletion-impact -> blocking @ 0.60 (n=73, validity 0.88; a dangling reference to a removed def/class/signature)\n- regression -> blocking @ 0.54 (base-reviewer dimension, n=307, validity 0.83) — NEW key\n- error-handling -> blocking @ 0.50 (base-reviewer dimension, n=238, validity 0.83) — NEW key\n`security` stays as-is; performance/docs/supply-chain/scope-intent and the high-volume dimensions stay advisory (insufficient evidence or high friction). The two `regression`/`error-handling` entries are BASE-REVIEWER dimensions (not glob overlays in OVERLAY_IDS): `exec`/`applies_to` are inert and only `default_posture`/`block_threshold`/`blocking_enabled` are consulted by `registry.threshold_for`.\n\nUpdate the three governance-pin tests that assert the exact approved blocking set (previously the 3-member {secret-detection, high-critical-security, security}) to the new 7-member set, so the \"adding a blocking criterion must be a deliberate re-approved change\" guard still holds at the new baseline.\n\n## Portability\nPure in-process threshold config consumed by `registry.threshold_for`; no CI provider or external trigger involved, so the change is fully portable across environments with diverse or no CI (project.portability unaffected).\n\n## Sequencing\nLand BEFORE RP-06 S1 (dietetic-pompous-boar, relates_to): S1 folds this packaged `criteria_routing.json` into an immutable CriteriaSnapshot golden, so S1 must derive its golden from the flipped file. S1 is still open, so no golden re-derivation is required here.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json — flip the four criteria (2 edited entries + 2 new base-dimension keys).\n- tests/unit/test_code_review_deletion_impact.py — repoint the deletion-impact routing assertion to (0.60, True).\n- tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py — expand the approved-blocking-set pin to the 7 members.\n- tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py — expand the approved-blocking-set pin to the 7 members.\n(The calibration/analysis harness under docs/experiments/ is a local investigation aid and is NOT part of this landing.)\n\n## Testing\n- The three updated governance tests pass and now pin the 7-member blocking set (any 8th addition must be deliberately re-approved).\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_deletion_impact.py tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py` green.\n- The broader code-review routing/registry unit tests stay green (no criterion resolves to a different threshold than declared).\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] api-compat, deletion-impact, regression, error-handling are blocking_enabled=true at 0.51/0.60/0.54/0.50 respectively in the packaged criteria_routing.json, each with a `_comment` citing cranial-goodly-seahog + the code-v3 calibration.\n- [x] `security` and the two DET detectors remain blocking; no other criterion is flipped (the approved blocking set is exactly 7 members).\n- [x] regression and error-handling are added as base-reviewer dimension entries (applies_to=[], only posture/threshold/blocking_enabled consulted).\n- [x] The three governance-pin tests assert the new 7-member set and pass.\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` are green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787117989695099001,"uuid":"c5ed6b36-e1e5-4764-a63d-72eea0691ea6"}